<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plŏcē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοκή</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In
			rhetoric, <i>a repeating of the same word with a
				different meaning</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 5,
				§ 532</span></i>; Jul. <i><span class="en">Rufin. p.
			236</span></i> Ruhnk. (ad <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 3, 41</span></i>, written as
			Greek).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			music, <i>a combining of different tones together</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9</span></i>,
			§§ 936, 958.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
